{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef bitset<128> u99;\n\nconstexpr const int mod = 1000000007;\nconstexpr const int inv = 570000004;\nconstexpr int add(int a, int b) { return a + b < mod ? a + b : a + b - mod; }\nconstexpr int sub(int a, int b) { return a < b ? a - b + mod : a - b; }\nconstexpr int mul(int a, int b) { return 1LL * a * b % mod; }\n\nunordered_map<u99, int> name;\nint n, dfn, son[65536][128];\nint dfs(u99 s) {\n    auto ite = name.find(s);\n    if (ite != name.end()) return ite->second;\n    int ret = dfn++;\n    name[s] = ret;\n    for (int i = 0; i != (1 << n); ++i) {\n        u99 t = s;\n        for (int j = 0; j != (1 << n); ++j) if (!t[j])\n            for (int k = i & j; k; k ^= k & -k) if (s[j ^ k & -k]) {\n                t[j] = 1;\n                break;\n            }\n        son[ret][i] = dfs(t);\n    }\n    return ret;\n}\n\nint p[7][7], q[7][1<<7], dp[8][1<<14]; // use max sizes\n\nint main() {\n    cin >> n;\n    dfs(1);\n    int m = 1 << n;\n    for (int i = 0; i != n; ++i) for (int j = 0; j != n; ++j) cin >> p[i][j], p[i][j] = mul(p[i][j], inv);\n    for (int i = 0; i != n; ++i) for (int j = 0; j != m; ++j) {\n        q[i][j] = 1;\n        for (int k = 0; k != n; ++k) q[i][j] = mul(q[i][j], j >> k & 1 ? p[k][i] : sub(1, p[k][i]));\n    }\n    memset(dp, 0, sizeof(dp));\n    dp[0][0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i != n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j != dfn; ++j) {\n            int cur = dp[i][j];\n            if (!cur) continue;\n            for (int k = 0; k != m; ++k) {\n                int nxt = son[j][k];\n                dp[i+1][nxt] = add(dp[i+1][nxt], mul(cur, q[i][k]));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    u99 res;\n    for (int i = 0; i != m; ++i) res[i] = 1;\n    cout << dp[n][name[res]] << endl;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int MOD = 1000000007;\n    static final int INV = 570000004;\n    static HashMap<BitSet, Integer> name = new HashMap<>();\n    static int n, dfn;\n    static int[][] son = new int[65536][128]; // max size\n    static int m;\n\n    static int add(int a, int b) {\n        int s = a + b;\n        return s < MOD ? s : s - MOD;\n    }\n\n    static int sub(int a, int b) {\n        return a < b ? a - b + MOD : a - b;\n    }\n\n    static int mul(int a, int b) {\n        return (int)((long)a * b % MOD);\n    }\n\n    static int dfs(BitSet s) {\n        Integer ite = name.get(s);\n        if (ite != null) return ite;\n        int ret = dfn++;\n        name.put((BitSet)s.clone(), ret);\n        for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {\n            BitSet t = (BitSet)s.clone();\n            for (int j = 0; j < m; ++j) {\n                if (!t.get(j)) {\n                    for (int k = i & j; k != 0; k ^= (k & -k)) {\n                        int bit = k & -k;\n                        if (s.get(j ^ bit)) {\n                            t.set(j);\n                            break;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            son[ret][i] = dfs(t);\n        }\n        return ret;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        n = sc.nextInt();\n        m = 1 << n;\n        BitSet init = new BitSet(128);\n        init.set(0);\n        dfs(init);\n        int totalStates = dfn;\n        int[][] p = new int[n][n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n                p[i][j] = sc.nextInt();\n                p[i][j] = mul(p[i][j], INV);\n            }\n        }\n        int[][] q = new int[n][m];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < m; ++j) {\n                q[i][j] = 1;\n                for (int k = 0; k < n; ++k) {\n                    q[i][j] = mul(q[i][j], (j >> k & 1) == 1 ? p[k][i] : sub(1, p[k][i]));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        int[][] dp = new int[n + 1][totalStates];\n        dp[0][0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < totalStates; ++j) {\n                int cur = dp[i][j];\n                if (cur == 0) continue;\n                for (int k = 0; k < m; ++k) {\n                    int nxt = son[j][k];\n                    dp[i + 1][nxt] = add(dp[i + 1][nxt], mul(cur, q[i][k]));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        BitSet res = new BitSet(128);\n        for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) res.set(i);\n        System.out.println(dp[n][name.get(res)]);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.9\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00020966715237591416, 0.0, 0.0, -5.864924969500862e-05, -6.007967749610543e-05, 0.0, -3.766942609217949e-05, -0.004340631887316704, -6.067568756407127e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -3.981510963058099e-05, -0.0007115454645827413, -1.5258672647178173e-05, -0.0024943212047219276, -0.05095884948968887, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.12692973017692566, 0.0, -1